seq='''<section id="sequence"><h2>2 · From an observed ball to a timed movement choice</h2>
<p>The eight lanes below are the same eight parts as the map. A <strong>state record</strong> contains current body angles and speeds, object tracks, touch, core context and control history. A <strong>command table</strong> contains simultaneous body, gaze and individual finger requests, one row per 50 ms. An <strong>intention</strong> names the tracked object and a desired body–object relationship, such as sustained hand control observed in earlier experience.</p>
<p>The top half specifies how the proposed system constructs and compares those tables. The lower half shows the joint changes needed in this particular illustrated example. Those lower labels describe the posed movement; they are not a six-stage routine to install in UEMA.</p>
<p><strong>Diagram key:</strong> q means joint angles. FK calculates connected bone positions from those angles. body[26,9] means 26 body targets with nine fields each: position, rotation, radius and strength. gaze[2] means the two eye-direction angles. joint_goal[J] holds named joint targets, including each finger joint; J is the number in the saved joint list. A mask says which requests are present. dt is the row's duration. Utility means the combined bodily benefit and cost; a continuation is the estimated benefit over the next three seconds.</p>
<p>Read top to bottom. On a narrow screen, scroll the diagram sideways. <a href="h84_whole_body_reach_20261026/movement_sequence.svg">Open the full diagram</a> · <a href="h84_whole_body_reach_20261026/movement_sequence.mmd">Mermaid source</a>.</p>
<div class="diagram-scroll" id="sequence-diagram" tabindex="0"><img class="sequence" src="h84_whole_body_reach_20261026/movement_sequence.svg" alt="Eight-part sequence: retrieve observed outcomes, vary concrete timed control fields, recurrently predict, score, dispatch and learn; followed by the illustrated body and finger changes."></div>
<div class="callout"><strong>What replaces “try different commands”:</strong> two rounds of 16 tables; perturb permitted movement coordinates, shift separate body/eye/finger boundaries by up to two 50 ms rows, forecast each row, keep four best, and execute only the best first row. The full field definitions and failure rules are in section 5. The sampling sizes are proposed settings, not measured performance.</div></section>'''
